# Demonstration mode and environment

Copy this file to `.env`, or export the values in your shell. All of these are optional for the
local development preview.

## Demonstration mode

Seeds the fictional village and enables `POST /demo/session`, which signs in as a seeded account
through the real login path. Not available in a deployable configuration.

```
SMARTGATE_DEMO=true
```

Leave it unset for real accounts. `NODE_ENV=production` is refused by this prototype.

## Server

```
PORT=4100
```

## First account (real mode)

Create the first platform administrator with an operator-controlled command:

```
SMARTGATE_OPERATOR_PASSWORD='a-long-passphrase' npm run setup:operator -- \
  --email operator@example.com --name "Operations lead"
```

The same account can be created over HTTP with a one-time token, but only while no platform
administrator exists. The token is cleared from the environment after use.

```
SMARTGATE_SETUP_TOKEN=
```

## Database

Use the migration role for `npm run migrate` and the application role for the API. See
[docs/postgresql.md](postgresql.md).

```
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://smartgate_app:PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:5432/smartgate
```

The deployable setting: verify the schema, never change it.

```
# SMARTGATE_SKIP_MIGRATIONS=true
```

Local development only: use embedded PostgreSQL on disk instead of a server.

```
# SMARTGATE_DATA_DIR=.data/postgres
```

## Edge controller

Edge-only settings belong in the separate `smartgate-edge` repository, not in the platform API
environment. A real controller claims a short-lived, one-time enrollment code, then stores its
unique credential in its local SQLite database. It must use HTTPS and an HOA-approved maximum
cached-configuration age. See the edge repository README for startup and rotation instructions.
